                <pb facs="0670" n="558" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg558"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No 3892.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to King Edward</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >The White House</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-01-16"><hi rendition="#italic">January 16,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I beg your Majesty to accept my own sympathy and that of the American people on
                    account of the dire disaster that has befallen your Majesty’s subjects in
                    Jamaica.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Theodore
                    Roosevelt.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
